> Port the original domino-board encoding into the core

A rectangular domino placement covers two adjacent board cells. Make
each cell a required column and each possible horizontal/vertical
placement a row. A selected exact cover is then precisely a tiling:
every cell is covered once, with no overlaps or gaps. Identical
dominoes do not need separate piece-identity columns. The reusable
builder keeps the original row-major cell order, adding a horizontal
placement before a vertical placement at each cell. Its first 4×6
tiling therefore keeps the original placement IDs.

For h,w>0 there are hw required cells and
h(w-1)+(h-1)w placements, each with two incidences. The 4×6 board
has 24 cells, 38 placements and 101 dancing-links nodes including
headers/root. Odd area makes a domino tiling impossible. For a full
rectangle, even area is also sufficient: one dimension is even, so
parallel domino strips construct a tiling. This sufficiency does not
extend to arbitrary boards with holes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/exact_cover_domino.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto problem=dm::algorithms::domino_exact_cover(4,6);const auto t=dm::algorithms::exact_cover_trace(problem.num_columns,problem.placements);
  std::print("Original 4x6: cells {}; placements {}; nodes {}; solved {}; dominoes {}; restored mesh {}.\n",problem.num_columns,problem.placements.size(),t.initial_nodes.size(),t.outcome.result.solved,t.outcome.result.rows.size(),t.initial_nodes==t.final_nodes);
  std::print("Selected placement IDs:");for(int row:t.outcome.result.rows)std::print(" {}",row);std::print(".\n\n");
  std::print("| board | cells | placement rows | solved | selected dominoes |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto [h,w]:std::vector<std::pair<int,int>>{{0,6},{1,1},{1,2},{2,3},{3,3},{4,6},{6,8}}){const auto p=dm::algorithms::domino_exact_cover(h,w);const auto r=dm::algorithms::exact_cover_work(p.num_columns,p.placements);std::print("| {}x{} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",h,w,p.num_columns,p.placements.size(),r.result.solved,r.result.rows.size());}
  dm::algorithms::domino_tiling_diagram(problem,t.outcome.result,90,1100).save_svg("build/exact_cover_domino.svg");
}
```
