> Equal node counts can hide very different search and history costs

Compare n singleton rows, one for each column, with one row containing
all n columns. Both matrices have n incidences and 2n+1 mesh nodes.
The singleton instance descends n levels, scanning n,n-1,...,1 active
headers, for n(n+1)/2 scans. The whole-universe row needs one column
choice, scanning n headers, and reaches its cover at depth one.
Both perform n covers and n uncovers. Singleton rows need no data-node
unlink writes; the whole row gives 4(n-1) data-link writes including
restoration. These counts come from the actual kernels below.

The sparse runtime mesh is linear in the problem representation, while
optional full residual snapshots can grow quadratically even on these
simple inputs. Under the capture convention in the next section, the
measured singleton history has (9n^2+23n+8)/2 entries, versus 10n+10
for the whole-row instance. The former follows by summing the full
n-column snapshot and actual partial-row depths over all choose,
select, solution, unselect and finished events. This is a property of
this trace format and these instances, not a universal search bound.
Minimum-size column selection also has a real scan cost; its heuristic
does not make general exact cover polynomial-time.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/exact_cover_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<double> sizes,scan_single,scan_whole,history_single,history_whole;
  std::print("| columns n | nodes in both | singleton scans | whole-row scans | singleton entries | whole-row entries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128}){std::vector<std::vector<int>> rows(n);std::vector<int> whole(n);for(std::size_t i=0;i<n;++i){rows[i]={int(i)};whole[i]=i;}const auto a=dm::algorithms::exact_cover_trace(n,rows),b=dm::algorithms::exact_cover_trace(n,{whole});
    if(a.outcome.work.column_scans!=n*(n+1)/2||b.outcome.work.column_scans!=n||a.captured_entries!=(9*n*n+23*n+8)/2||b.captured_entries!=10*n+10||a.initial_nodes.size()!=b.initial_nodes.size())throw std::runtime_error("known exact-cover family failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,a.initial_nodes.size(),a.outcome.work.column_scans,b.outcome.work.column_scans,a.captured_entries,b.captured_entries);sizes.push_back(std::log2(n));scan_single.push_back(std::log2(a.outcome.work.column_scans));scan_whole.push_back(std::log2(b.outcome.work.column_scans));history_single.push_back(std::log2(a.captured_entries));history_whole.push_back(std::log2(b.captured_entries));}
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(sizes,scan_single,"singleton",{37,99,235}).points(sizes,scan_single,"",{37,99,235},5).line(sizes,scan_whole,"whole row",{220,38,38}).points(sizes,scan_whole,"",{220,38,38},5).title("Actual minimum-column header scans").x_label("log2(required column count n)").y_label("log2(actual header scans)");
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(sizes,history_single,"singleton",{37,99,235}).points(sizes,history_single,"",{37,99,235},5).line(sizes,history_whole,"whole row",{220,38,38}).points(sizes,history_whole,"",{220,38,38},5).title("Optional snapshots have their own cost").x_label("log2(required column count n)").y_label("log2(logical captured entries)");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,520).title("Same sparse node count, different depth, heuristic work and history").fit_panels().save_svg("build/exact_cover_work.svg");
}
